# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env template for Zapstore publishing (zsp)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Read by `zsp publish` in the last step of the release workflow. This
# file is gitignored — never commit the real .env.
#
# On the maintainer's self-hosted runner, both release workflows read the
# populated file from $CRUXCOACH_SECRETS_DIR/.env (see CONTRIBUTING.md →
# "Releases & CI (maintainer only)"). It is parsed as literal zsp KEY=value
# data and MUST NOT be sourced as shell: a bunker URL contains `&`, which is
# a shell control operator. Do not add shell quotes either; zsp treats them as
# part of the value. For a local publish dry-run, place your value here and
# invoke `zsp publish` manually.
#
# The exact variables zsp consumes depend on the tool's version — always
# check `zsp --help` and https://github.com/franzaps/zapstore-cli for the
# authoritative list. At the time of writing, at minimum:

# Preferred for unattended CI: a previously authorised NIP-46 bunker whose
# cached zsp client key belongs to the runner user. The URL's public key must
# match zapstore.yaml's pubkey exactly.
# SIGN_WITH=bunker://<64-char-publisher-hex>?relay=wss://relay.example&secret=<connection-secret>

# Alternative: the publisher's Nostr secret key. This is headless, but places
# the irreplaceable publisher key in a file/environment. Never use a bare npub
# (zsp only emits unsigned events) or `browser` (requires human NIP-07 approval).
# SIGN_WITH=nsec1...
